<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22169" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnambŭlātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		inambulo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A walking up and down</i> on the rostra (of
			orators; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rare but class.),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 3, 15, 27</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut. 43, 158</span></i>. — <b>Poet.</b>: tremuli lecti, <i>a
				moving</i> or <i>shaking to and fro</i>, <i><span class="en">Cat. 6,
			11</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a place to walk
			in</i>, <i>a walk</i>, <i>promenade</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 1, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 1,
				3, § 11</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
